<title>AUSTRALIA: SFE wheat futures fall slightly.</title>
<headline>SFE wheat futures fall slightly.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheat futures settled slightly lower on Thursday, with the January contract down A$1.00 and spot July down A$7.50.</p>
<p>Grains traders said the January decline was due to likely hedge selling, with the market expecting some gains in the short-term.</p>
<p>The Australian market was generally mirroring the U.S., but would maintain a small premium until more widespread rains were seen.</p>
<p>The July spot market contract declined with less demand for feed and on arbitrage dealing, traders said.  </p>
